                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1402-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_hc.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Hypercardioid" title="Hypercardioid" ></span>Audix f6</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Hypercardioid Dynamic Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Audix f6 is a large-diaphragm dynamic for kick drum.</p><p>The f6 is part of the new &#8220;fusion&#8221; series, a lower cost alternative to the company&#8217;s popular D series microphones. The previous fusion series was built overseas, the new line is assembled and tested in USA.</p><blockquote><p><cite>Electronic Musician, 2011</cite><br />Designed expressly for kick drums, the f6 has a huge scoop in the midrange, so it provides plenty of low end with a rising high end around 5kHz that captures the beater attack on each hit &#8212; without the midrange mush. The net effect is an aggressive kick sound that&#8217;s reminiscent of a <a href="http://recordinghacks.com/microphones/Shure/Beta-52A">Shure Beta 52</a>. Like its sibling, the <a href="http://recordinghacks.com/microphones/Audix/D6" >Audix D6</a>, there&#8217;s little need to add EQ with the f6 on kick; it&#8217;s plug-and-play, giving you exactly what you need in a hurry.</p></blockquote><p><p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Audix/f6">Audix f6</a></p>
